Claude Code subagent definitions go here, and stay the exception rather than the rule.

Unlike skills, subagents have no cross-vendor standard — the Agent Skills spec covers
skills only — so anything written here works in Claude Code and nowhere else. When a
task could be expressed either way, write a skill in .agents/skills/ instead.

A subagent earns its place on mechanics a skill cannot give it: its own tool allowlist,
a context window isolated from the main conversation, or a different model. Never on
what it knows — conventions live in AGENTS.md, and a copy of them drifts.
